{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bigospeedrun/verifier/pulls/20","id":4922274054,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVDiv6M8AAAABJWPxBg","html_url":"https://github.com/bigospeedrun/verifier/pull/20","diff_url":"https://github.com/bigospeedrun/verifier/pull/20.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/bigospeedrun/verifier/pull/20.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bigospeedrun/verifier/issues/20","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bigospeedrun/verifier/pulls/20/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bigospeedrun/verifier/pulls/20/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bigospeedrun/verifier/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bigospeedrun/verifier/issues/20/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bigospeedrun/verifier/statuses/cd95de596dcecb0745c9509ad70ed9e8825ee816","number":20,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"statement: Heilbronn triangle with the saving as a parameter","user":{"login":"joshuacortez","id":7113605,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTM2MDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7113605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuacortez","html_url":"https://github.com/joshuacortez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuacortez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuacortez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuacortez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuacortez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuacortez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuacortez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuacortez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuacortez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuacortez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Status: statement** (lean-statements track). This proposes a trusted target for the [Heilbronn triangle board](https://bigospeedrun.com/other/heilbronn-triangle). It is not a proof submission.\n\n## What this adds\n\n- `challenges/heilbronn-triangle/`, following `docs/new-statements.md`:\n  - `Statement.lean`: `BigOSpeedrun.HeilbronnTriangle.Bound (η : ℚ)`, which says there are `c > 0` and `N` such that for every `n ≥ N` some `n`-point set in `[0,1]²` has every triangle area `≥ c · n^(-2+η)`. This is the board's claim \"Δ(n) ≥ c·n^(-2+η) for every sufficiently large n\". Larger `η` is better.\n  - OpenAI's `OAI/Geometry/HeilbronnTriangle/Definitions.lean`, frozen byte for byte from `openai/math@1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a`, with `provenance.json`, `LICENSE` (Apache-2.0) and `NOTICE`.\n- `auto-research/lean-statements/2026-10-19-joshuacortez-heilbronn-triangle/`: the model comparison, the places the statement could be vacuous, rejected drafts, and Lean vacuity checks.\n\n## Why a new statement\n\nThe upstream comparator target `OAI.Problem355.heilbronn_power_lower_bound` claims point sets only along a subsequence `n_j → ∞`, with constant `1`, at one fixed exponent. That is weaker than the board's \"every sufficiently large n\" in one respect and fixes `c = 1` in another, so it can't represent the board. The record repository littleBro/heilbronn-triangle-bounds notes the same mismatch. Only the upstream *definitions* are reused.\n\n## Vacuity checks (Lean, standard axioms only)\n\n- `bound_zero : Bound 0`: the classical `Δ(n) ≥ n⁻²/8` for all `n ≥ 1`, via Erdős's parabola mod a Bertrand prime.\n- `bound_mono`: a larger saving implies every smaller one.\n- `not_bound_of_two_lt : 2 < η → ¬ Bound η`.\n- `nonvacuous : Bound 0 ∧ ¬ Bound 3`.\n\n`#print axioms` gives `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` for all four.\n\n## Local check\n\nBuilt with Lean 4.34.1 and Mathlib `d13f23b`, the pins in `profiles/lake-manifest.json`: no errors, no warnings, no `sorry`. The Mathlib cache was unreachable from the build machine, so Mathlib was compiled from source with only the needed modules. For that run, the frozen file's `import Mathlib` was swapped for narrower Mathlib imports, and nothing else changed. `verify.sh` builds the exact committed files with the normal cache. Its hash and upstream byte-identity steps were run and pass. A build of the exact committed files with the full `import Mathlib` is running now, and I'll post its output in a comment here.\n\n## Not claimed / open obligations\n\n- No board record is proved. All rows stay Claimed, and no evidence label changes.\n- Maintainers still need to review the model and add the profile, target generator, form option and receipt bindings. Comparator, wrong-bound rejection and the axiom audit still need to run in the trusted pipeline.\n- The equivalence between the witness-set form and `Δ(n) ≥ a` (the supremum is attained, by compactness) is argued, not formalized.\n\nProcess note: `AGENTS.md` says \"local review only … do not open PRs\", while `auto-research.md` asks agents to open one focused PR. I read the first as applying to verifier development. If statement PRs should wait, please say so and I'll convert this to a draft.\n\nThe statement was also checked by a separate review pass. It found no blockers, and its should-fix points are applied: the citation of the baseline preprint's definition, the corrected meaningful range `0 ≤ η ≤ 5/6`, and the module-layout note.\n\nPrepared by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) working for @joshuacortez; disclosed in `NOTICE.md`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0159zhcq8r8CNzAFgwauTzai\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-19T14:09:46Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T18:37:05Z","closed_at":"2026-10-21T18:37:05Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e795b4566113f08944f7a503f8180bdacdb43aa2","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"